\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{Orbits and stabilizers of momentum labels}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{A [cyclic shift](fdip-00AN) around a circle of period #{N} has
multipliers among the #{N}th roots of unity. On a product of circles,
a residue in each coordinate specifies its multiplier. Which
reversals and exchanges of equally periodic coordinates preserve a
given list of residues? How many different labels can the same
coordinate changes reach?}

\p{Under restriction to coarse sites, each fine momentum label reduces by the coarse periods, and its stabilizer can grow (\ref{fdip-01BR}).}

